// PIN FMT-002 — the export block stays where the author put it.
//
// Imports were printed first unconditionally, while `#> { … }` was placed in
// source order relative to the STATEMENTS only. So a module that opens with its
// export block and imports underneath came back with the two swapped — a token
// reordering the gate refused, which left fourteen application files
// unformattable, among them every `api/` re-export layer in GO and Chaturanga.
//
// A formatter reorders nothing.
//
// Underscores in the name and not the `FMT-002` the other pins use: a module's
// name has to be an identifier and has to match its file stem (E001), so this
// one pin cannot spell its own ID the way the rest do.
# FMT_002_orden_del_bloque_de_exportacion {

    #> {
        saluda
    }
    <# std/math => m

    saluda() { <~ m::abs(-1) }
}
